  margin: 2rem auto;
}

.vimeo-responsive.square {
  padding-bottom: 100%;
  max-width: 600px;
  margin: 2rem auto;
}

@media (max-width: 768px) {
  .vimeo-responsive.portrait,
  .vimeo-responsive.square {
    max-width: 90%;
  }
}
&lt;/style&gt;

&lt;strong&gt;by keya singh and ioanna loup&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;
the body provides us a sensual experience of itself, others and the world. in return, it demands care and concern – often requiring professional intervention. with its roots in mark fisher’s texts about “the eerie”, this film explores such interventions with a focus on ophthalmology and one patient’s inner voice during those interventions. the eerie is the failure of presence and the failure of absence. and our eyes contribute to these failures.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
